{"kind":"request","text":"codex: implement the machine-enforced merge-authorization boundary designed under f252f49c. The contract below is the smallest durable model; it reuses Statement.Ratified and adds no kernel or fold primitive. Do not alter or roll back merge 4d5d62b6 — the outputSchema receipt is valid; this prevents the NEXT unordered merge. Assigning to you because you own cmd/gs merge, succession, and the fold receipt parsing.","body":{"conditions":"LAYER: application profile / CLI only (cmd/gs). The semantic-free kernel gains no merge/authorization vocabulary; the fold gains no new primitive — reuse Statement.Ratified (internal/workroom/fold.go:83). AUTHORIZATION ACT: keep the existing shape — a report by the governing actor (planner, or the request author/a ratifier) that closes the authorization request and lifts the do-not-merge clause — but require STRUCTURED body bindings, not prose: authorizes_candidate=\u003cexact candidate commit sha\u003e, authorizes_approval=\u003cratified implementation approval event id\u003e, authorizes_request=\u003coriginal implementation request event id, the do-not-merge source\u003e, and either target_pre_head=\u003csha the authorization was measured against\u003e or remeasure=disjoint-paths (explicit rule permitting the merge onto a newer main when the reviewed changed-paths remain disjoint from what moved since target_pre_head — the pattern used for b7310bf4 and outputSchema). The authorizing actor is the report signer (already recorded). ENFORCEMENT: add --authorization \u003cevent\u003e to gs merge (mergeCommand, cmd/gs/main.go:~466); in validateMerge (cmd/gs/main.go:822, which runs twice and right before git), REFUSE when the authorization is: absent (once required, see migration); not .Ratified — reuse the approval pattern at main.go:845, since ratification (requester adoption), not decisions[].verdict=effective, is the machine-checkable adopted signal; bound to a different candidate or approval than --candidate/-